# Password storage
#
Password secure storage is done using Argon2id. The parameters have been chosen using the utility
argon2calibrate provided by Crypt::Argon2 (see SECURITY file for more information).
What type of hash? [argon2id]
How many threads may it use [1]
How much memory may it use (e.g. 32M) 20M
How much time may argon2 take? (in milliseconds) 100
type = argon2id
threads = 1
mem_cost = 20M
time_cost = 48

The salt size is 16 bytes (recommended by RFC9106).

# Email API

Set an expiration date for the API tokens, 3 months.

